# 3. NON-NEGOTIABLE DOMAIN OWNERSHIP MODEL

Every domain must have a distinct logical responsibility, explicit public interfaces, permitted dependencies and test ownership.

The domains must remain separate even though the frontend is a single React application and Supabase is the shared backend.

**Separate logical domains do not mean separate databases, separate deployments or separate authentication systems.**

Maintain:

- One application.
- One canonical identity system.
- One established Supabase backend.
- One authorized shared data authority.
- Existing Browser and Telegram integration.
- Existing account and approval policies.

## Required domain mapping

| Domain | Canonical responsibility | May consume | Must not own |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Calendar** | School events, audiences, responses, cancellation and event lifecycle | Academics assignment scope, Identity, Access Control | Attendance marks, class membership mutations, Parent Notes |
| **Class Community** | Class announcements, homework, questions, replies, moderation and class media references | Academics scope, Media interfaces, Access Control | Independent roster authority, Calendar lifecycle, private messaging |
| **Parent Notes** | Parent-originated notes, Teacher recipient selection, replies, quota and sending-window workflow | Family verified links, Academics Teacher assignments, Identity | Academic remarks, Attendance corrections, Messaging threads |
| **Messaging** | Authorized operational threads, participants, replies and read acknowledgements | Identity, approved recipient/scope interfaces | Parent Notes quota or academic grading |
| **Directory** | Explicitly approved public Teacher/Administration card publication | People verified presentation projection | Account approval, private personnel identity mutation |
| **Food Menu** | School meal content, weekly menus and approved publication lifecycle | School staff permissions, Media where approved | Attendance, Family relationships, student health records |
| **Preferences** | Authorized user/application preference settings | Identity account reference | School policy, account approval, domain business rules |
| **Notifications** | Notification projection, destinations, read state and delivery integration | Approved domain event references | Underlying Enrollment, Attendance, Calendar or Governance decisions |
| **Public Content** | Approved public information and public inquiry entry points | Directory, Food Menu and other public read projections | Private school/student records |
| **Academics** | Academic years, levels, classes, subjects, class membership and Teacher assignments | People identity references, Identity and Access Control | Assessment marks, Attendance registers, Enrollment decisions |
| **People** | Canonical student/staff identity and permitted identity details | Explicit Identity account association, approved academic references | Account credentials, implicit guardian authority, class assignment ownership |
| **Enrollment** | Applications, admission review, document requirements and authorized enrollment operations | People, Family, Academics and Media contracts | Account approval, invented pupil identities, unauthorized class placement |
| **Public Inquiry** | Public inquiry submission, staff review and response lifecycle | Public context, authorized staff identity | Enrollment applications, internal messaging, school account creation |
| **Students search and identity readers** | Authorized People-owned student directory and identity projections | Academics membership read projection, approved Access Control | Duplicated student records, independent roster storage, grades and guardian mutation |

### Important distinction

**Students search is not a new competing student-identity domain.**

Students search and identity readers belong to the People domain as a dedicated read capability.

They may consume authorized Academics membership projections to display class/year history.

They must not introduce a second `students` authority.

Similarly:

- Notification delivery is not a new authority for the underlying event.
- Public Directory is not the private staff-personnel record.
- Academic Performance is not an independent grading authority.
- Attendance may reference class membership but does not own it.
- Enrollment may coordinate approved domain operations but must not create competing canonical records.

These distinctions must be visible in the code structure and interfaces.

