### Rules for module creation

1. Search for an existing canonical owner before adding a module.
2. Preserve existing tested modules when they already provide the correct boundary.
3. One feature module must have one coherent responsibility.
4. A module may contain several related functions when they implement the same contract.
5. Do not create one file per trivial helper merely to reduce line counts.
6. Do not create an empty directory or placeholder module.
7. Do not create a generic domain manager that imports all other domains.
8. Do not use deep relative imports to bypass public interfaces.
9. Avoid circular domain dependencies.
10. Do not move server authorization policy into frontend modules.
11. Do not introduce another Supabase client instance.
12. Preserve existing typed RPC contracts.
13. Use explicit module interfaces.
14. Preserve actual error semantics and result shapes.
15. Do not change business behavior during a pure structural extraction.

A domain boundary is valid only if its implementation and consumers obey the intended ownership.

